1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,794
This is needle seagrass, Halodule pinifolia.

2
00:00:03,014 --> 00:00:05,423
A display, not a scan of a meadow in Mati.

3
00:00:05,803 --> 00:00:08,647
Each leaf is fine, with one dark vein down the centre.

4
00:00:09,197 --> 00:00:10,466
Watch the tip.

5
00:00:10,746 --> 00:00:14,140
That vein splits in two, and the tip stays rounded.

6
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:19,688
That rounded tip is how you tell it from the other needle seagrass,
Halodule uninervis, whose tip is a trident.

7
00:00:20,068 --> 00:00:23,242
The rhizome is usually pale, with clean black leaf scars.

8
00:00:23,422 --> 00:00:26,001
The patch spreads when the buried stem grows through the sand.

9
00:00:26,161 --> 00:00:27,820
Roots grow down at each node.

10
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:29,899
It can also flower and set seed.
